 "course": "gasvalue",
 "sources": {
  "beginner": "NextGen FlareExplorer (panels/gasvalue/FlareExplorer.jsx): the gas sheet (fractions, carbon number, molar mass, heating value, liquid density) and the flare boxes are all editable, so ERIEMU can be typed in; it prints heating value, gpm and kg/Mscf with fmt.f4 and flare tonnes with fmt.t3 (gasvalueLab.js:221-232), exactly the precisions the prompt asks. Each is also a hand-calc taught in beginner m02-m05.",
  "intermediate": "NextGen RouteExplorer 'year' view (RouteExplorer.jsx:170-205, editable parcel, yield, recovery, price, reference plant and costs) prints capital d2, product f4, valuePerMscf f4. Its gas is preset-only (EGBEMA/OGUTA/studio, RouteExplorer.jsx:432), so the ADIBAWA flare CO2e comes from FlareExplorer (t3) x the 0.87 recovery, net abatement adds the two typed tonnages, and the breakeven is the closed form (hurdle less margin) over net abatement taught in intermediate m05/l02.",
  "advanced": "NextGen RolloutExplorer (panels/gasvalue/RolloutExplorer.jsx): vessel (basis select), vaporizer, carousel, bank, cascade and switch modes all take typed inputs and print f4, cascade kg t3, matching the prompt's precisions. Z by DAK is engine-only, so the bank and cascade need the panel (gauge readings plus 1.013 typed as bar(a), taught in advanced m03/l03)."
 },
